#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100694 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315"}] :question/id #uuid "66ec04a0-2af8-5187-98b2-b06eedd5b0a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4406" :question/problem "Find $CD$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}2}} \\times \\color{#2E8B57}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{#2E8B57}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{#2E8B57}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}2}}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}2}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}2}}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nCD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100695 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100873 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71ff07eb-2e16-529e-b17c-1bf7cb9703bd"}] :question/id #uuid "3a696ed3-e341-5ea6-bf17-681ba8e386c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4407" :question/problem "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The full matrix product is\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row in $A$ by the $2$nd column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100741 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd"}] :question/id #uuid "c3ed8d05-758d-5ae0-bf57-3779fde6020b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5885" :question/problem "Compute the product\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -5 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}3}} \\times {\\color{#2E8B57}\\fbox{1}} {\\color{#2E8B57}\\checkmark} {\\color{#2E8B57}\\fbox{1}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}2}} = \n\t\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{black}2}}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}\n       -1  \\\\\n \t0  \\\\\n        -2\n    \\end{bmatrix}\n\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n        2 & -5\n    \\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & = \n\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n        (-1)\\cdot 2 & (-1)\\cdot (-5)  \\\\\n        0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot (-5) \\\\\n        (-2)\\cdot 2 & (-2)\\cdot (-5)\n    \\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\n\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n       -2 & 5  \\\\\n       0 &  0  \\\\\n       -4 &  10 \n    \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407 :topic/title "Multiplying Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "802f0864-9cf0-558a-a018-182bdf8634b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097948} {:answer/id #uuid "b691c70f-2540-52ab-8dcd-df9ba3df2032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097949} {:answer/id #uuid "fe65f2af-0005-5919-8f19-ecf1b9c126a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 14 \\\\ 14 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097950} {:answer/id #uuid "1c72920d-772a-500b-9395-f0209f18233d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 14 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097951}